From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:05:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] fix(app-css): read only tokens the palette writes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Red: a-palette-the-app-never-reads
  POSITIVE every token the app reads is one the palette defines
    (culprit c219da21) -> missing ["--danger", "--media-warm"]
  POSITIVE a token read with no fallback is one the palette guarantees
    (culprit f8cf0852) -> bare ["--media-warm"]

Decision: R. The guard is the owner's class-level fix for "two parties
that must agree on a vocabulary"; two new reads drifted past it.

  c219da21  the ledger error read var(--danger,#c44). No palette and no
            generated stylesheet defines --danger, so it could only ever
            resolve to #c44 while claiming to follow a token.
  f8cf0852  the media stats read var(--media-warm) with no fallback. It is
            defined under .kind-media only, but read under .media-workspace,
            which every image-led collection gets: outside the media kind
            the declaration had no value and was dropped in silence.

Fix: the ledger error is a literal #c44, like every other error colour in
the file (.err, .calc-error, .btn.danger). The media kind names its warm
as its own --secondary (both themes), and the even-figure rule is scoped
to .kind-media, the only place that value exists. It is NOT widened to the
derived --secondary for other collections: that token has no dark value
and measured as low as 1.92:1 on dark grounds (#2f34c6, "real estate
listings with images").

Live, computed in chromium from fileAppCss()+fileLedgerCss() over
paletteCss(buildPalette('اعمل لي متجر قهوة مختصة')), before -> after:
  media light      even rgb(189, 89, 56)  -> rgb(189, 89, 56)
  media dark       even rgb(240, 138, 102) -> rgb(240, 138, 102)
  inventory light  even rgb(65, 47, 37)   -> rgb(65, 47, 37)
  inventory dark   even rgb(65, 47, 37)   -> rgb(65, 47, 37)
  ledger error     rgb(204, 68, 68)       -> rgb(204, 68, 68)
No computed colour changes; only the reads of unwritten tokens go.

Non-vacuity (mutate the fix back, guard goes red, restore):
  palette-danger: ledger reads var(--danger,#c44) again
    ✕ POSITIVE — every token the app reads is one the palette defines
    + Array [ "--danger" ]   RESTORED: sha256 identical
  palette-media-warm: even figure reads var(--media-warm) again
    ✕ POSITIVE — every token the app reads is one the palette defines
    ✕ POSITIVE — a token read with no fallback is one the palette guarantees
    + Array [ "--media-warm" ] (both)   RESTORED: sha256 identical

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CSeapUrWatvdumdAwyPuqV
